      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "If the starter is experiencing problems, it may be due to over- or under-colonization by lactobacilli or yeast, contamination, or other factors. A bad batch of bacteria can lead to an overgrowth of unwanted microorganisms, which can cause off-flavors, mold, or slimy texture. If you notice visible signs of mold, sliminess, or an unusual color, it's likely the starter is compromised. Additionally, changes in pH, temperature, or feeding schedule can also stress the starter and lead to undesirable growth.",
